    "result_text": "The full build is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the customerCode de-duplication rule as a new, self-contained pipeline step rather than modifying existing code.\n\n**New file** \u2014 `DeduplicateOwnerCustomerCode.java`: a single small function with no surrounding class context (WMC_other = 0) and low cyclomatic complexity. It gathers existing owners' codes and, if the computed code collides, appends `-<n>` with the smallest `n \u2265 2` that is unique, then writes it back to the owner. Since the owner isn't saved yet, its own code is absent from the store, so no self-exclusion logic is needed.\n\n**Wiring** \u2014 `owners.POST.yml`: inserted a `deduplicateCustomerCode` step (under the same `transaction` governance) between `assignCustomerCode` and `save`, so the de-duplicated code is what gets persisted and returned.\n\nThis keeps structural impact minimal: no existing method's body or complexity grew (`AssignOwnerCustomerCode` is untouched), and the change is two files \u2014 one new cohesive unit plus the YAML wiring. The acceptance test (`coreCustomerCodesStayUnique`) and the full suite pass.",
